<concept base="Anywhere" id="t00730">
	<title>Rearview</title>
	<conbody>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e02411">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="1" outputclass="formatc" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="0">
						<entry colname="col1" colsep="0">
							<fig id="e02412">
								<figgroup>
									<image align="center" href="../../images/N_CT25Z132.eps" scale="95" placement="break"/>
								</figgroup>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2">
							<p>(2) View switching button</p>
							<p>(3) Back button</p>
						</entry>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e02413">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="1" outputclass="formatc" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="0">
						<entry colname="col1" colsep="0">
							<fig id="e02414">
								<figgroup>
									<image align="center" href="../../images/N_CT25E082.eps" scale="95" placement="break"/>
								</figgroup>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2">
							<p>(4) infotainment system power button</p>
						</entry>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<section>
			<title>Operating conditions</title>
			<p>The Rear View function will turn on under the following conditions:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<p>Shifting the gear to R (Reverse).</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>Pressing the Parking/View button (1) while P (Park), N (Neutral) or D (Drive) and the vehicle speed is slower than 10 km/h (6 mph)</p>
				</li>
			</ul>
			<p>Pressing the View switching button (2) with the Rear top view on the screen allows you to select rear top view, rearview, or rear wide view.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<title>Off conditions</title>
			<p>The Rear View while driving function will turn off under the following conditions while parking:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<p>Shifting the gear to P (Park)</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>Pressing the Parking/View button (1)</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>Pressing the back button (3) on the rear monitor screen</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>Pressing the infotainment system operation button (4)</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>N (Neutral) or D (Drive) and the vehicle speed is faster than 10 km/h (6 mph)</p>
				</li>
			</ul>
			<note type="note">
				<p>Rear View will not turn off when the vehicle is in R (Reverse).</p>
			</note>
		</section>
	</conbody>
</concept>